  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://davidkoepsell.com/bfo-agent/working#BehaviorAloneCannotInstantiateRolePrinciple">
    <work4:type rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031"/>
    <work:comment rdf:resource="http://davidkoepsell.com/bfo-agent/working#Asserts that behavioral manifestation (BehavioralLegalManifestation) alone is insufficient to instantiate a role (BFO_0000023); additional normative, recognitional, or social grounding conditions must obtain."/>
    <work:comment rdf:resource="http://davidkoepsell.com/bfo-agent/working#A role (BFO_0000023) is an externally-grounded realizable entity that inheres in a bearer; its instantiation requires not merely behavioral patterns (BehavioralLegalManifestation, a process) but also social, institutional, or normative recognition. Behavior alone is a process (BFO_0000015) and insufficient to constitute the specifically dependent continuant that is a role."/>
    <obo:BFO_0000050 rdf:resource="http://davidkoepsell.com/bfo-agent/working#RecognitionOriginThesis"/>
  </rdf:Description>
